/-
# Finite-prefix / cross-tail closure for the computed BF4 floor

Let `E_k` majorize the physical-minus-terminal-smoothed entry error and let
`F_k > 0` be the automatically computed finite ideal floor.  The desired
estimate is `E_k / F_k <= 1/2048` at every cutoff.  It is enough to check a
finite prefix and prove on the remaining tail

  E_(k+1) * F_k <= E_k * F_(k+1).

The cross inequality is division-free.  It is suitable for symbolic
polynomial proofs or rigorous interval certificates, while exact prefix
values may be generated by Rust, C, or Python and rechecked by Lean.
-/

import YMGap.Continuum.BF4BoundaryMessageComputedTerminalFloor
import YMGap.Continuum.BF4BoundaryMessageRelativeErrorCrossTail

namespace YMGap.Continuum.BF4BoundaryMessageComputedFloorCrossTail

set_option maxRecDepth 100000
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000

open YMGap.Constructive
open YMGap.Continuum.BF4AnchoredProjectiveProfileHarnack
open YMGap.Continuum.BF4BoundaryMessageComputedTerminalFloor
open YMGap.Continuum.BF4CalibratedProfileHarnack
